From 82fd25a5477054a0727ab920701b7555898586b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:31:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: let a vulnerability cancel the matching permanent
 resistance

The borg noted fire, cold, electricity and acid vulnerabilities (for
example from the burning up, chilled to the bone or steelskin curses)
only to lower the value of its gear; its resistance traits stayed set.
In the game a vulnerability takes away one level of permanent resistance
unless immune (calc_bonuses()), so one resistance plus a vulnerability
leaves none, and the borg's danger estimate divided that element's
damage by three when the game would not.

Clear the permanent resistance trait when a vulnerability cancels it.
Temporary resistance is counted separately, as before.
---
 src/borg/borg-trait.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-trait.c b/src/borg/borg-trait.c
index 154eb3849..5bac81478 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-trait.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-trait.c
@@ -2167,6 +2167,20 @@ static void borg_notice_equipment(void)
         && borg.trait[BI_RLITE])
         borg.trait[BI_RBLIND] = true;
 
+    /* A vulnerability (such as the burning up, chilled to the bone or
+     * steelskin curse) takes away one level of the permanent resistance
+     * to that element unless immune (calc_bonuses()), so a single
+     * resistance and a vulnerability leave none.  Temporary resistance is
+     * counted separately (borg.temp). */
+    if (borg.trait[BI_CRSFVULN] && !borg.trait[BI_IFIRE])
+        borg.trait[BI_RFIRE] = false;
+    if (borg.trait[BI_CRSCVULN] && !borg.trait[BI_ICOLD])
+        borg.trait[BI_RCOLD] = false;
+    if (borg.trait[BI_CRSEVULN] && !borg.trait[BI_IELEC])
+        borg.trait[BI_RELEC] = false;
+    if (borg.trait[BI_CRSAVULN] && !borg.trait[BI_IACID])
+        borg.trait[BI_RACID] = false;
+
     /*** Quiver needs to be evaluated ***/
 
     /* Ignore invalid missiles */
